{%- comment -%}
  Usage: {% render 'fabric-surface', image: product.featured_image, alt: '…',
                                     ratio: '3 / 4', caption: fabric_sub %}

  Renders the photograph of a real product. There is deliberately no woven
  texture stand-in: a CSS weave is a picture of cloth nobody photographed, and
  it reads as stock we hold. Until the photo is there the surface stays an
  empty ground with the fabric's own line on it.

  The srcset is built by hand rather than with image_tag, and never asks for a
  width the source does not have. image_tag's `widths` on a small image is one
  of the ways a Liquid error ends up printed into the page — and when that
  happens inside the product page's JSON payload it takes the whole gallery
  down with it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign ratio = ratio | default: '1 / 1'
  assign sizes = sizes | default: '(max-width: 700px) 50vw, 25vw'
  assign loading = loading | default: 'lazy'
-%}
<div class="surface" style="aspect-ratio: {{ ratio }};">
  {%- if image -%}
    {% render 'responsive-img', image: image, alt: alt, sizes: sizes, loading: loading %}
  {%- else -%}
    <div class="blank">
      {%- if caption != blank -%}<span class="hand">{{ caption }}</span>{%- endif -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
  {{ overlay }}
</div>
